  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {即位|そくい}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ (ascend the throne)\n- {即位|そくい}⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{礼|れい}→礼：02170_rei⟧ (enthronement ceremony)\n- {即位|そくい}{式|しき} (coronation ceremony)\n- {即位|そくい}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{祝|いわ}う→祝う：01881_iwau⟧ (celebrate the enthronement)\n\nUSAGE:\nIn Japanese context, {即位|そくい} refers specifically to the Emperor's accession. The formal ceremony is called {即位|そくい}⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{礼|れい}→礼：02170_rei⟧ ({即位礼正殿|そくいれいせいでん}⟦の→の：09472_no⟧{儀|ぎ} in its full form). The most recent enthronement was in 2019 when Emperor Naruhito ascended to the Chrysanthemum Throne. The word can also be used for foreign monarchs.",
